{"type": "step", "node_id": 23, "parent_node_id": 22, "role": "assistant", "content": "## Solution\n\n**Setup.** Place Ω with center O at the origin, radius 10. Let A = (−10, 0) and X = (10, 0), so AX is a diameter.\n\n**Locating C.** Write C = (10 cos θ, 10 sin θ). Then\n$$AC^2 = (10\\cos\\theta+10)^2 + (10\\sin\\theta)^2 = 200(1+\\cos\\theta) = 400\\cos^2(\\theta/2).$$\nSince AC = 16, we get cos(θ/2) = 4/5, sin(θ/2) = 3/5. Hence\n$$\\cos\\theta = \\tfrac{7}{25},\\quad \\sin\\theta = \\tfrac{24}{25},\\quad C = \\left(\\tfrac{14}{5}, \\tfrac{48}{5}\\right) = \\left(\\tfrac{350}{125}, \\tfrac{1200}{125}\\right).$$\n\n**Finding D.** We compute CX = 12. We need D = (10 cos φ, 10 sin φ) on Ω with CD = 12:\n$$CD^2 = 200 - 56\\cos\\varphi - 192\\sin\\varphi = 144 \\implies 7\\cos\\varphi + 24\\sin\\varphi = 7.$$\nWriting this as 25 cos(φ − α) = 7 with cos α = 7/25, sin α = 24/25: the solution φ = 0 gives X; the other is φ = 2α, giving\n$$\\cos 2\\alpha = -\\tfrac{527}{625},\\quad \\sin 2\\alpha = \\tfrac{336}{625},\\quad D = \\left(-\\tfrac{1054}{125}, \\tfrac{672}{125}\\right).$$\n\n**Reflections.** Midpoint of AC: M₁ = (−18/5, 24/5) = (−450/125, 600/125).\n$$D' = 2M_1 - D = \\left(\\tfrac{154}{125}, \\tfrac{528}{125}\\right).$$\n\nMidpoint of CD: M₂ = (−352/125, 936/125).\n$$X' = 2M_2 - X = \\left(-\\tfrac{1954}{125}, \\tfrac{1872}{125}\\right).$$\n\n**Area of △CD′X′.** Using C = (350/125, 1200/125):\n$$D' - C = \\left(-\\tfrac{196}{125}, -\\tfrac{672}{125}\\right),\\quad X' - C = \\left(-\\tfrac{2304}{125}, \\tfrac{672}{125}\\right).$$\n$$\\det = \\tfrac{(-196)(672) - (-672)(-2304)}{125^2} = \\tfrac{-672(196+2304)}{15625} = \\tfrac{-1{,}680{,}000}{15625}.$$\n$$\\text{Area} = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\cdot\\tfrac{1{,}680{,}000}{15625} = \\tfrac{840{,}000}{15625} = \\tfrac{1344}{25}.$$\n\nSince 1344 = 2⁶·3·7 and 25 = 5², gcd(1344, 25) = 1. Thus p = 1344, q = 25, and\n\n$$p + q = \\boxed{1369}.$$\n\n### PROOF COMPLETE", "thinking": "Let me solve this geometry problem carefully.\n\nCircle Ω with radius 10, so diameter AX = 20. C lies on Ω with AC = 16. D is the other point on Ω such that CX = CD. D' is reflection of D across midpoint of AC. X' is reflection of X across midpoint of CD. Find area of triangle CD'X'.\n\nLet me set up coordinates. Place the circle with center O at origin, radius 10. Let A and X be endpoints of a diameter. Let me put A = (-10, 0) and X = (10, 0). So AX is along x-axis, center at origin.\n\nC is on Ω with AC = 16. C = (10cos θ, 10 sin θ) for some angle θ. AC = distance from A=(-10,0) to C.\n\nAC² = (10cosθ + 10)² + (10sinθ)² = 100(cosθ+1)² + 100sin²θ = 100(cos²θ + 2cosθ + 1 + sin²θ) = 100(2 + 2cosθ) = 200(1+cosθ) = 400cos²(θ/2).\n\nAC = 20|cos(θ/2)| = 16, so cos(θ/2) = 4/5 (taking positive). So θ/2 has cos = 4/5, sin = 3/5.\n\nSo cos θ = 2cos²(θ/2) - 1 = 2(16/25) - 1 = 32/25 - 1 = 7/25.\nsin θ = 2 sin(θ/2)cos(θ/2) = 2(3/5)(4/5) = 24/25.\n\nSo C = (10·7/25, 10·24/25) = (70/25, 240/25) = (14/5, 48/5).\n\nLet me verify: C = (2.8, 9.6). |C| = √(7.84 + 92.16) = √100 = 10. ✓\n\nAC = distance from (-10,0) to (14/5, 48/5) = √((14/5+10)² + (48/5)²) = √((64/5)² + (48/5)²) = √((4096+2304)/25) = √(6400/25) = 80/5 = 16. ✓\n\nNow X = (10, 0). CX = distance from C to X = √((10 - 14/5)² + (0 - 48/5)²) = √((36/5)² + (48/5)²) = √((1296+2304)/25) = √(3600/25) = 60/5 = 12.\n\nSo CX = 12. We need D on Ω, D ≠ X (the other point), with CD = CX = 12.\n\nSo D is on the circle and CD = 12. The points on Ω at distance 12 from C: X is one, D is the other.\n\nLet me find D. D = (10cos φ, 10 sin φ) with CD = 12.\nCD² = (10cosφ - 14/5)² + (10sinφ - 48/5)² = 144.\n\nExpand: 100cos²φ - 2·10cosφ·14/5 + (14/5)² + 100sin²φ - 2·10sinφ·48/5 + (48/5)² = 144.\n\n100 - (56)cosφ - (192)sinφ + (196 + 2304)/25 = 144.\n\nWait let me recompute: 2·10·(14/5) = 28·... let me be careful.\n\n2·10cosφ·(14/5) = 2·10·(14/5)cosφ = 56cosφ.\n2·10sinφ·(48/5) = 2·10·(48/5)sinφ = 192sinφ.\n\n(14/5)² + (48/5)² = (196+2304)/25 = 2500/25 = 100.\n\nSo: 100 - 56cosφ - 192sinφ + 100 = 144.\n200 - 56cosφ - 192sinφ = 144.\n56cosφ + 192sinφ = 56.\nDivide by 8: 7cosφ + 24sinφ = 7.\n\nFor X: cosφ = 1, sinφ = 0: 7·1 + 0 = 7. ✓\n\nWe need the other solution. 7cosφ + 24sinφ = 7. Write as R cos(φ - α) = 7 where R = √(49+576) = √625 = 25, tan α = 24/7.\n\nSo cos(φ - α) = 7/25 where cos α = 7/25, sin α = 24/25.\n\nφ - α = ±arccos(7/25). One solution: φ - α = 0 → φ = α, giving cosφ = 7/25, sinφ = 24/25, which is C itself! Wait, that gives point C. But C has CD = 0, not 12. Let me check: if φ = α, then D = (10·7/25, 10·24/25) = C. Then CD = 0 ≠ 12. But plugging in: 7·(7/25) + 24·(24/25) = (49+576)/25 = 625/25 = 25 ≠ 7. \n\nHmm, that's not 7. So φ = α is NOT a solution. Let me redo.\n\ncos(φ - α) = 7/25. Solutions: φ - α = ±β where cos β = 7/25.\n\nFor X = (10,0): cosφ = 1, sinφ = 0. 7cosφ + 24sinφ = 7. So 7·1+24·0 = 7 ✓. So φ_X = 0. Then φ_X - α = -α, and cos(-α) = cos α = 7/25 ✓.\n\nOther solution: φ - α = +α → φ = 2α. So D corresponds to φ = 2α where cos α = 7/25, sin α = 24/25.\n\ncos(2α) = 2cos²α - 1 = 2(49/625) - 1 = 98/625 - 1 = -527/625.\nsin(2α) = 2sinα cosα = 2(24/25)(7/25) = 336/625.\n\nSo D = (10·(-527/625), 10·336/625) = (-5270/625, 3360/625) = (-527/62.5, ...). Let me simplify: 10/625 = 2/125.\n\nD = (-527·2/125, 336·2/125) = (-1054/125, 672/125).\n\nLet me verify D is on circle: (-1054/125)² + (672/125)² = (1054² + 672²)/125². \n1054² = 1110916. 672² = 451584. Sum = 1562500. 125² = 15625. 1562500/15625 = 100. ✓ |D| = 10.\n\nVerify CD = 12: C = (14/5, 48/5) = (350/125, 1200/125). D = (-1054/125, 672/125).\nCD² = ((350+1054)/125)² + ((1200-672)/125)² = (1404/125)² + (528/125)² = (1404² + 528²)/125².\n1404² = 1971216. 528² = 278784. Sum = 2250000. /15625 = 144. √144 = 12. ✓\n\nGreat. So:\n- A = (-10, 0) = (-1250/125, 0)\n- X = (10, 0) = (1250/125, 0)\n- C = (350/125, 1200/125)\n- D = (-1054/125, 672/125)\n\nNow, midpoint of AC: M_AC = ((-10 + 14/5)/2, (0 + 48/5)/2) = ((-50/5 + 14/5)/2, 48/10) = ((-36/5)/2, 24/5) = (-18/5, 24/5) = (-450/125, 600/125).\n\nD' = reflection of D across M_AC: D' = 2·M_AC - D.\nD' = 2(-450/125, 600/125) - (-1054/125, 672/125) = (-900/125 + 1054/125, 1200/125 - 672/125) = (154/125, 528/125).\n\nMidpoint of CD: M_CD = ((350 - 1054)/(2·125), (1200 + 672)/(2·125)) = (-704/250, 1872/250) = (-352/125, 936/125).\n\nX' = reflection of X across M_CD: X' = 2·M_CD - X = 2(-352/125, 936/125) - (1250/125, 0) = (-704/125 - 1250/125, 1872/125) = (-1954/125, 1872/125).\n\nNow triangle CD'X' with vertices:\n- C = (350/125, 1200/125)\n- D' = (154/125, 528/125)\n- X' = (-1954/125, 1872/125)\n\nArea = (1/2)|det[D'-C, X'-C]|.\n\nD' - C = (154-350, 528-1200)/125 = (-196, -672)/125.\nX' - C = (-1954-350, 1872-1200)/125 = (-2304, 672)/125.\n\ndet = (-196)(672) - (-672)(-2304) = -196·672 - 672·2304 = -672(196 + 2304) = -672·2500 = -1680000.\n\nAll over 125² = 15625.\n\nArea = (1/2)·|−1680000|/15625 = 840000/15625.\n\nSimplify: 840000/15625. Divide both by 625: 840000/625 = 1344. 15625/625 = 25. So 1344/25.\n\nCheck gcd(1344, 25): 1344 = 2^6 · 3 · 7 = 64·21 = 1344. 25 = 5². gcd = 1.\n\nSo area = 1344/25, p = 1344, q = 25, p + q = 1369.\n\nLet me double-check the determinant computation.\n\nD' - C = (-196/125, -672/125)\nX' - C = (-2304/125, 672/125)\n\ndet = (-196/125)(672/125) - (-672/125)(-2304/125)\n= [(-196)(672) - (-672)(-2304)] / 125²\n= [-196·672 - 672·2304] / 15625\n= -672(196 + 2304) / 15625\n= -672 · 2500 / 15625\n= -1680000 / 15625\n\nArea = (1/2)(1680000/15625) = 840000/15625 = 1344/25.\n\np + q = 1344 + 25 = 1369.\n\nLet me verify 840000/15625: 15625 · 50 = 781250. 840000 - 781250 = 58750. 15625 · 3 = 46875. 58750 - 46875 = 11875. 15625 doesn't go into 11875 evenly... hmm let me just do the division properly.\n\n840000 / 15625: 15625 = 5^6. 840000 = 84 · 10000 = 84 · 10^4 = 2^4 · 3 · 7 · 5^4 · ... wait.\n\n840000 = 84 · 10000 = (4·21)·(10^4) = 2^2 · 3 · 7 · 2^4 · 5^4 = 2^6 · 3 · 7 · 5^4.\n15625 = 5^6.\n\n840000/15625 = 2^6 · 3 · 7 · 5^4 / 5^6 = 2^6 · 3 · 7 / 5^2 = 1344/25. ✓\n\ngcd(1344, 25): 1344 = 2^6 · 3 · 7, 25 = 5^2. Coprime. ✓\n\np + q = 1369.\n\nLet me also double check the reflection computations once more.\n\nA = (-10, 0), C = (14/5, 48/5).\nMidpoint of AC = ((-10 + 14/5)/2, 48/10) = ((-50+14)/(10), 24/5) = (-36/10, 24/5) = (-18/5, 24/5). ✓\n\nD = (-1054/125, 672/125).\nD' = 2(-18/5, 24/5) - (-1054/125, 672/125) = (-36/5, 48/5) - (-1054/125, 672/125).\n-36/5 = -900/125. -900/125 + 1054/125 = 154/125. ✓\n48/5 = 1200/125. 1200/125 - 672/125 = 528/125. ✓\nD' = (154/125, 528/125). ✓\n\nC = (350/125, 1200/125), D = (-1054/125, 672/125).\nMidpoint of CD = ((350-1054)/250, (1200+672)/250) = (-704/250, 1872/250) = (-352/125, 936/125). ✓\n\nX = (10, 0) = (1250/125, 0).\nX' = 2(-352/125, 936/125) - (1250/125, 0) = (-704/125 - 1250/125, 1872/125) = (-1954/125, 1872/125). ✓\n\nAll checks out. The answer is 1369.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786630837}
